// ReconGlobals.cpp -- storage for the unresolved data symbols.
//
// GENERATED by tools/gen-recon-globals.py from the unresolved-symbol list in
// build/msbuild6.log and the `extern <type> <name>;` declarations in the tree.
// Do not edit by hand; re-run the generator instead. The class statics at the
// bottom are hand-written (the generator skips them).
//
// These are not constants. In the TV build each one is a word (or a small
// struct) in the uninitialised data that the code fills in at runtime: the
// resource manager assigns the resource ids, the app stores its singletons and
// the framework keeps its statics there. Zero-initialised storage is what the
// binary holds before that code runs, so it is the correct initial value, and
// it is what makes the references resolve.
//
// The type of every definition below is copied from the tree's own
// declaration: the mangled name encodes it, so a different type would produce
// a different symbol and leave the reference unresolved.
//
// Some of the names below are vtable slots rather than plain data. A zero word
// links and stores, but the first virtual call through that object reads entry
// zero of the table and jumps to null. Those definitions are left zero; the
// recovered slot counts are in tools/off-function-tables.txt.
//
// 776 definitions follow (762 from `extern` declarations, 14 written by hand).

